      "writtenOn": "2022-10-05T21:23:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `KeyParameter` is a KeyMint specific type, we need something more generic for other HALs which may implement rollback functionality. I was under the impression that the caller of RKPD would serialize the expected parameters before sending it to RKPD, which would forward it through this HAL interface.\n\nSo I guess the call flow would have been\n```\nks2 / system (serializes) -\u003e rkpd -\u003e IRPC (deserializes) -\u003e KeyMint / other HAL\n```\n\nBut I guess that would require the underlying vendor service in IRPC to know what serialization format to expect from the system code, which would then require another format on top of AIDL, which seems silly now that I type it all out.\n\nI suppose no other HAL would really need to have rollback protection, due to the device wide rollback protection KeyMint already provides. In which case it would be safe to then just directly use the proper KeyMint type here.\n\n@sethmo@google.com do you have any thoughts on this, since you\u0027re writing this portion of RKPD? It may make more sense to going back to letting the caller domain just handle the key upgrade flow outside of RKPD, and then pass those results back in.",
      "parentUuid": "60565073_91afec8e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 490,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 490,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "694c86f1f2aa30645b3eafe298f6025c55ff0416",
